# --- Pekopeko: non-maintained / temporary working files ---
# These are working artifacts from AI-assisted sessions, not part of the
# durable spec. The durable continuity doc is docs/ROADMAP.md — that one
# stays tracked and should be kept up to date and committed.

# One-off context dump generated once at the start of a session; not meant
# to be kept up to date. See docs/ROADMAP.md instead.
docs/PROJECT_HANDOFF.md
docs/qwen-reports/*.md

# Per-phase prompt packages handed to a coding LLM (qwen, etc.) to execute
# a batch of fixes/tasks. Disposable once that phase is done. Covers
# docs/qwen-phase0-prompts.md and any future docs/qwen-phaseN-prompts.md.
docs/qwen-*-prompts.md

# Generic convention for any other scratch/working file from an AI session
# (use these suffixes/prefixes for throwaway notes so they never need a
# manual .gitignore update).
*-scratch.md
_tmp_*

# Intermediate reasoning drafts from qwen's abandoned Task E attempt
# (audit_summary.md, capabilities_mapping.md, incorrect_citations.md,
# requirements_analysis.md) — dead working files, not part of the corpus.
# See docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 0 for what actually happened with Task E.
temp/

# pytest-cov's binary coverage database — regenerated by every test run,
# never meant to be versioned.
.coverage

# --- Pekopeko: local device secrets (TASK-004, app/config) ---
# .env holds secrets/local overrides for the PEKOPEKO_* config keys — never
# committed. .env.example (the template) stays tracked.
.env
